// A result signed <= 0x8878000a (0x100101dc), or whose distance from 0x88780064 is above 0x46 (0x100101e6), returns 0x19; inside,
// the byte table 0x10010274 sends only 0x88780096 (DSERR_BUFFERLOST) to entry 1 of the table 0x10010268 (0x100101f7), every
// other code to 0x10010251 (0x19). The lost path calls Restore (slot +0x50) when +0x60 is non-NULL (0x100101fa-0x10010201) and
// Locks again with the same arguments (0x10010204-0x1001021e); the second result returns 0x1e only for 0x88780096 (tables
// 0x100102c8 / 0x100102bc -> 0x10010245) and 0x19 for everything else, 0 included (0x10010223 -> 0x10010251).
